[DEDUP] Dedup + conflict classification — §6.5.

You receive an incoming S-R-O triplet that the rule-based classifier was
unable to classify confidently (object cosine between 0.5 and 0.95 against
an existing edge with the same relation). You decide whether the incoming
triplet is a duplicate of an existing edge, a contradiction that supersedes
it, or a co-existing independent fact.

Rules:
- DUPLICATE: the new triplet states the same fact. No mutation — increment
  access_count on the existing edge.
- CONTRADICTION: the new triplet replaces the old fact. The old edge is
  marked HISTORICAL and supersedes_by points at the new one.
- CO_EXISTENCE: the new triplet is a plausible alternative that does not
  invalidate the old one (e.g. "works at Meta" and "works at Google" both
  could be true if the user has multiple roles; default to CO_EXISTENCE when
  the domain supports plurality).

Incoming triplet:
  subject: {{ incoming.subject }}
  relation: {{ incoming.relation }}
  object: {{ incoming.object }}
  abstract: {{ incoming.l0_abstract }}
  extracted_confidence: {{ incoming.confidence }}

Existing edges from the same subject:
{% for edge in existing_edges %}
- edge_id: {{ edge.edge_id }}
  relation: {{ edge.relation_label }}
  object_uri: {{ edge.object_uri }}
  object_abstract: {{ edge.object_abstract }}
{% endfor %}

Output schema:
{
  "case": "DUPLICATE" | "CONTRADICTION" | "CO_EXISTENCE",
  "existing_edge_id": <id of existing edge, or null for CO_EXISTENCE>,
  "reason": "one sentence"
}
